ous compliance with evolving market regulations. Effective robotic process automation not only prevents robotic process anomalies but also supports the company's strategic decision-making processes. [Data: Sources (3757, 3758, 1303), Date_Range ((2023, 01, 01), (2023, 12, 12))]", "# SAP BTP Security and Compliance Overview as of 2025\n\nThis report delves into SAP BTP's key security and compliance features, illustrating how these entities interact within the organizational framework to uphold regulatory standards and manage security risks effectively. The information is relevant to the company's operations around 2025.\n\n## Risk Management Operational Scope\n\nThe SAP Authorization and Trust Management service at SAP BTP plays a pivotal role in identifying, assessing, and mitigating security risks. Their proactive approach, highlighted from the beginning of 2025, helps safeguard SAP BTP against potential security pitfalls and ensures continuous compliance with evolving security regulations. Effective risk management not only prevents security anomalies but also supports the company's strategic decision-making processes. [Data: Sources (1018, 1968), Date_Range ((2025, 01, 01), (2025, 04, 17))]\n\n## Cloud Integration for Data Services Security Features\n\nCloud Integration for Data Services at SAP BTP ensures that all data integrations adhere to the security standards set by regulatory bodies. Their focus on data security and compliance, noted starting 2025, is crucial in maintaining SAP BTP's reputation and operational security, especially in managing sensitive data and integrations. Their efforts underscore the commitment to upholding high security standards and best practices. [Data: Sources (131, 1548), Date_Range ((2025, 01, 01), (2025, 04, 17))]\n\n## Interdepartmental Collaboration for Compliance\n\nCollaboration between the SAP Authorization and Trust Management service, Cloud Integration for Data Services, and other security-related components, established in 2025, ensures that security measures are effective and compliant. This synergy is vital for holistic security and has been instrumental in integrating security with compliance strategies at SAP BTP. Enhanced interdepartmental cooperation during this period plays a crucial role in aligning the company's strategies with regulatory requirements. [Data: Sources (3604, 3605), Date_Range ((2025, 01, 01), (2025, 04, 17))]", "# SAP Pricing Service and Variant Configuration Overview as of 2025\n\nThis report delves into SAP's key services focusing on pricing and variant configuration, illustrating how these entities interact within the organizational framework to provide accurate and efficient pricing solutions. The information is relevant to the company's operations around 2025.\n\n## Pricing Service Operational Scope\n\nThe Pricing Service at SAP plays a pivotal role in identifying, assessing, and mitigating financial risks. Their proactive approach, highlighted from the beginning of 2025, helps safeguard SAP against potential financial pitfalls and ensures continuous compliance with evolving market regulations. Effective risk management not only prevents financial anomalies but also supports the company's strategic decision-making processes. [Data: Sources (1, 2), Date_Range ((2025, 01, 01), (2025, 11, 12))]\n\n## Variant Configuration and Governance\n\nThe Variant Configuration Department ensures that all SAP's operations adhere to the legal standards set by regulatory bodies. Their focus on corporate governance and contract management, noted starting Q2 2024, is crucial in maintaining SAP's reputation and operational legality, especially in managing complex contracts and corporate agreements. Their efforts underscore the commitment to upholding high legal standards and ethical practices. [Data: Source (2553), Date_Range ((2024, 07, 24), (2025, 11, 12))]\n\n## Interdepartmental Collaboration for Compliance\n\nCollaboration between the Pricing Service and Variant Configuration Departments, established in Q2 2024, ensures that risk mitigation strategies are legally sound and that compliance measures consider financial risks. This synergy is vital for holistic governance and has been instrumental in integrating risk management with legal compliance strategies at SAP. Enhanced interdepartmental cooperation during this period plays a crucial role in aligning the company's strategies with regulatory requirements. [Data: Sources (2554), Date_Range ((2024, 07, 24), (2025, 11, 12))]\n\n## New Features and Enhancements\n\nThe Pricing Service has introduced several new features and enhancements, including support for dynamic scale base types, condition exclusion on condition record level, and customizing API to return the scales order. These updates aim to improve the accuracy and efficiency of pricing calculations, ensuring that SAP's customers receive the best possible pricing solutions. [Data: Sources (2555, 2556, 2557), Date_Range ((2024, 07, 24), (2025, 11, 12))]\n\n## Deprecation and Removal of Features\n\nThe Pricing Service has deprecated and removed several features, including the LogParser API, to improve the overall stability and performance of the service. This change aims to reduce the risk of errors and ensure that SAP's customers receive the best possible pricing solutions. [Data: Source (16), Date_Range ((2025, 07, 17), (2025, 11, 12))]\n\n## Technical Updates and Maintenance\n\nThe Pricing Service has undergone several technical updates and maintenance, including the introduction of new APIs and the improvement of existing ones. These updates aim to improve the accuracy and efficiency of pricing calculations, ensuring that SAP's customers receive the best possible pricing solutions. [Data: Sources (2558, 1488, 1489, 1490), Date_Range ((2024, 12, 17), (2025, 11, 12))]", "# SAP Technology and Pricing Service Overview as of 2025\n\nThis report provides an overview of SAP's key technology and pricing services, highlighting their core attributes, connections, and noteworthy claims. The information is relevant to SAP's operations around 2025.\n\n## SAP Pricing Service Operational Scope\n\nThe SAP Pricing Service plays a pivotal role in identifying, assessing, and mitigating financial risks. Their proactive approach, highlighted from the beginning of 2025, helps safeguard SAP against potential financial pitfalls and ensures continuous compliance with evolving market regulations. Effective risk management not only prevents financial anomalies but also supports the company's strategic decision-making processes. [Data: Sources (8, 9), Date_Range ((2025, 01, 01), (2025, 11, 12))]\n\n## SAP Variant Configuration and Pricing\n\nSAP Variant Configuration and Pricing is a critical component of SAP's technology and pricing services, ensuring accurate handling of time-dependent conditions and supporting dynamic scale base types as part of the pricing input. This allows the correct evaluation of scale conditions based on the input during runtime rather than relying only on predefined customizing. [Data: Sources (23, 24), Date_Range ((2025, 01, 01), (2025, 11, 12))]\n\n## Interdepartmental Collaboration for Compliance\n\nCollaboration between SAP's technology and pricing services, established in 2025, ensures that risk mitigation strategies are legally sound and that compliance measures consider financial risks. This synergy is vital for holistic governance and has been instrumental in integrating risk management with legal compliance strategies at SAP. Enhanced interdepartmental cooperation during this period plays a crucial role in aligning the company's strategies with regulatory requirements. [Data: Sources (35, 36), Date_Range ((2025, 01, 01), (2025, 11, 12))]", "# SAP BTP Community Overview as of 2025\n\nThis report delves into the key components and features of SAP BTP, highlighting how these entities interact within the organizational framework to provide a comprehensive platform for businesses. The information is relevant to the company's operations around 2025.\n\n## SAP Build Work Zone Features and Updates\n\nSAP Build Work Zone is a key component of SAP BTP, offering a range of features and updates to support businesses in their digital transformation journey. The platform provides AI-powered tools for text generation and summarization, as well as a new set of features for workpage management. Effective use of SAP Build Work Zone can help businesses streamline their operations and improve productivity. [Data: Sources (110, 330), Date_Range ((2025, 01, 01), (2025, 09, 04))]\n\n## Variant Configuration Updates and Enhancements\n\nVariant Configuration is another critical component of SAP BTP, providing a range of updates and enhancements to support businesses in their product configuration and pricing needs. The platform offers improved performance, new features, and enhanced functionality to help businesses streamline their operations and improve customer satisfaction. [Data: Sources (1501, 1502, 1503, 1504, 1505), Date_Range ((2025, 02, 05), (2025, 09, 04))]\n\n## Cloud Identity Services Updates and Enhancements\n\nCloud Identity Services is a key component of SAP BTP, providing a range of updates and enhancements to support businesses in their identity and access management needs. The platform offers improved security, new features, and enhanced functionality to help businesses streamline their operations and improve customer satisfaction. [Data: Sources (316, 318, 319, 320), Date_Range ((2025, 07, 22), (2025, 09, 04))]", "# SAP Pricing Service and Related Components Overview as of 2025\n\nThis report delves into SAP's key components focusing on the Pricing Service, Migration Assessment, and related entities, illustrating how these entities interact within the organizational framework to provide pricing and related services effectively. The information is relevant to SAP's operations around 2025.\n\n## Pricing Service Operational Scope\n\nThe Pricing Service at SAP plays a pivotal role in identifying, assessing, and mitigating financial risks. Their proactive approach, highlighted from the beginning of 2024, helps safeguard SAP against potential financial pitfalls and ensures continuous compliance with evolving market regulations. Effective risk management not only prevents financial anomalies but also supports the company's strategic decision-making processes. The Pricing Service supports various standard pricing routines and has been enhanced with new features such as currency conversion, determination, and extensions concept. [Data: Sources (3001, 3002), Date_Range ((2024, 01, 01), (2025, 05, 21))]\n\n## Migration Assessment and Related Components\n\nThe Migration Assessment component at SAP ensures that the company's operations are up to date with the latest market regulations. Their focus on dual-stack scenarios, software version updates, and other related features is crucial in maintaining SAP's reputation and operational legality, especially in managing complex contracts and corporate agreements. Their efforts underscore the commitment to upholding high legal standards and ethical practices. [Data: Sources (2051, 2052), Date_Range ((2024, 10, 26), (2025, 05, 21))]\n\n## Interdepartmental Collaboration for Compliance\n\nCollaboration between the Pricing Service and related components, established in 2024, ensures that risk mitigation strategies are legally sound and that compliance measures consider financial risks. This synergy is vital for holistic governance and has been instrumental in integrating risk management with legal compliance strategies at SAP. Enhanced interdepartmental cooperation during this period plays a crucial role in aligning the company's strategies with regulatory requirements. [Data: Sources (3003, 3004), Date_Range ((2024, 04, 15), (2025, 05, 21))]", "# SAP Pricing Service Overview as of July 2024\n\nThis report delves into the key features and updates of the SAP Pricing Service, highlighting its capabilities, enhancements, and changes as of July 2024. The information is relevant to the SAP ecosystem and its users.\n\n## Pricing Service Enhancements\n\nThe SAP Pricing Service has undergone significant enhancements, including the introduction of new APIs, improved condition determination, and enhanced scalability. These updates aim to improve the overall pricing experience for SAP users, making it more efficient and effective. The Pricing Service now supports standard requirement formulas, condition exclusions, and cost conditions, among other features. These enhancements demonstrate SAP's commitment to continuously improving its Pricing Service to meet the evolving needs of its users. [Data: Sources (2553, 2554, 2555), Date_Range ((2024, 06, 28), (2024, 07, 24))]\n\n## Condition Determination and Exclusion\n\nThe SAP Pricing Service has introduced new features to improve condition determination and exclusion. The service now considers condition records with exclusion indicators, ensuring that conditions are accurately determined and applied. This enhancement is crucial for ensuring that pricing calculations are accurate and compliant with regulatory requirements. [Data: Sources (2553, 2554), Date_Range ((2024, 06, 28), (2024, 07, 24))]\n\n## API Enhancements and Scalability\n\nThe SAP Pricing Service has introduced new APIs to improve scalability and usability. The service now supports APIs for testing local extensions, returning scales order, and considering cost conditions as external conditions. These enhancements aim to improve the overall pricing experience for SAP users, making it more efficient and effective. [Data: Sources (2555, 2556, 2557), Date_Range ((2024, 06, 28), (2024, 07, 24))]", "# SAP Technology Overview as of 2024\n\nThis report delves into SAP's key departments focusing on technology, illustrating how these entities interact within the organizational framework to uphold regulatory standards and manage financial risks effectively. The information is relevant to the company's operations around 2024.\n\n## SAP Build Process Automation Operational Scope\n\nThe SAP Build Process Automation Department at SAP plays a pivotal role in identifying, assessing, and mitigating financial risks. Their proactive approach, highlighted from the beginning of 2024, helps safeguard SAP against potential financial pitfalls and ensures continuous compliance with evolving market regulations. Effective risk management not only prevents financial anomalies but also supports the company's strategic decision-making processes. [Data: Sources (290, 291), Date_Range ((2024, 01, 01), (2024, 10, 02))]\n\n## Cloud Identity Services and Governance\n\nThe Cloud Identity Services Department ensures that all SAP's operations adhere to the legal standards set by regulatory bodies. Their focus on corporate governance and contract management, noted starting Q2 2024, is crucial in maintaining SAP's reputation and operational legality, especially in managing complex contracts and corporate agreements. Their efforts underscore the commitment to upholding high legal standards and ethical practices. [Data: Source (2813), Date_Range ((2024, 06, 05), (2024, 10, 02))]\n\n## Interdepartmental Collaboration for Compliance\n\nCollaboration between the SAP Build Process Automation and Cloud Identity Services Departments, established in Q2 2024, ensures that risk mitigation strategies are legally sound and that compliance measures consider financial risks. This synergy is vital for holistic governance and has been instrumental in integrating risk management with legal compliance strategies at SAP. Enhanced interdepartmental cooperation during this period plays a crucial role in aligning the company's strategies with regulatory requirements. [Data: Sources (2183, 2189), Date_Range ((2024, 06, 05), (2024, 10, 02))]", "# SAP BTP Community Overview as of 2025\n\nThis report delves into the key components of the SAP BTP community, focusing on the interactions between various departments and their impact on the organizational framework. The information is relevant to the company's operations around 2025.\n\n## Variant Configuration Operational Scope\n\nThe Variant Configuration Department at SAP BTP plays a pivotal role in identifying, assessing, and mitigating financial risks. Their proactive approach, highlighted from the beginning of 2025, helps safeguard SAP BTP against potential financial pitfalls and ensures continuous compliance with evolving market regulations. Effective risk management not only prevents financial anomalies but also supports the company's strategic decision-making processes. [Data: Sources (738, 813, 814, 815, 953), Date_Range ((2025, 01, 01), (2025, 05, 21))]\n\n## Graph and Identity Provisioning Department Collaboration\n\nCollaboration between the Graph and Identity Provisioning Departments ensures that risk mitigation strategies are legally sound and that compliance measures consider financial risks. This synergy is vital for holistic governance and has been instrumental in integrating risk management with legal compliance strategies at SAP BTP. Enhanced interdepartmental cooperation during this period plays a crucial role in aligning the company's strategies with regulatory requirements. [Data: Sources (816, 817, 2661, 2662, 2663), Date_Range ((2024, 07, 02), (2025, 05, 21))]\n\n## Kyma Runtime and Graph Department Updates\n\nThe Kyma Runtime and Graph Departments have been working together to update the Istio module to version 1.25.3 and 1.10.0 respectively. This update has improved the compatibility version parameters and has enabled the deletion of the annotation disable-external-name-alias. The Graph Department has also added new features to the Graph UI for business data graph configuration. [Data: Sources (818, 1893, 1895, 2668), Date_Range ((2024, 11, 18), (2025, 05, 21))]", "# SAP BTP and Kyma Runtime Overview as of 2024-12-19\n\nThis report delves into SAP BTP and Kyma Runtime's key components, focusing on their interactions and updates within the organizational framework to enhance operational efficiency and compliance. The information is relevant to the company's operations around 2024-12-19.\n\n## SAP BTP and Kyma Runtime Operational Scope\n\nSAP BTP and Kyma Runtime play a pivotal role in identifying, assessing, and mitigating technological risks. Their proactive approach, highlighted from the beginning of 2024, helps safeguard SAP against potential technological pitfalls and ensures continuous compliance with evolving market regulations. Effective risk management not only prevents technological anomalies but also supports the company's strategic decision-making processes. [Data: Sources (216, 1545), Date_Range ((2024, 12, 12), (2024, 12, 19))]\n\n## Kyma Runtime and SAP BTP Updates\n\nKyma Runtime and SAP BTP have been updated to enhance operational efficiency and compliance. The updates include new features such as zone-based podAntiAffinity rules for the istio-ingressgateway and istios Deployments, and the addition of new parameter sets to false, including PILOT_ENABLE_IP_AUTOALLOCATE. These updates underscore the commitment to upholding high operational standards and ethical practices. [Data: Sources (1707, 1708), Date_Range ((2024, 12, 12), (2024, 12, 19))]\n\n## Interdepartmental Collaboration for Compliance\n\nCollaboration between Kyma Runtime and SAP BTP, established in 2024, ensures that risk mitigation strategies are operationally sound and that compliance measures consider technological risks. This synergy is vital for holistic governance and has been instrumental in integrating risk management with operational compliance strategies at SAP. Enhanced interdepartmental cooperation during this period plays a crucial role in aligning the company's strategies with regulatory requirements. [Data: Sources (1706, 1709), Date_Range ((2024, 12, 12), (2024, 12, 19))]", "# SAP Cloud Services Overview as of 2025\n\nThis report delves into SAP's key cloud services, illustrating how these entities interact within the organizational framework to provide a comprehensive suite of cloud-based solutions. The information is relevant to SAP's operations around 2025.\n\n## Cloud Identity Services Operational Scope\n\nThe Cloud Identity Services at SAP play a pivotal role in managing user identities and access to cloud-based applications. Their proactive approach, highlighted from the beginning of 2025, helps safeguard SAP against potential security pitfalls and ensures continuous compliance with evolving regulatory standards. Effective identity management not only prevents security anomalies but also supports the company's strategic decision-making processes. [Data: Sources (1241, 1242, 1243), Date_Range ((2025, 01, 01), (2025, 05, 21))]\n\n## Cloud Integration and Governance\n\nThe Cloud Integration Department ensures that all SAP's cloud-based operations adhere to the integration standards set by regulatory bodies. Their focus on central store-based provisioning, noted starting 2025, is crucial in maintaining SAP's reputation and operational legality, especially in managing complex integrations and cloud-based agreements. Their efforts underscore the commitment to upholding high integration standards and ethical practices. [Data: Source (1316), Date_Range ((2025, 02, 25), (2025, 05, 21))]\n\n## Interdepartmental Collaboration for Integration\n\nCollaboration between the Cloud Identity Services and Cloud Integration Departments, established in 2025, ensures that identity management strategies are integrated with cloud-based integration measures. This synergy is vital for holistic governance and has been instrumental in integrating identity management with cloud-based integration strategies at SAP. Enhanced interdepartmental cooperation during this period plays a crucial role in aligning the company's strategies with regulatory requirements. [Data: Sources (1241, 1242, 1243), Date_Range ((2025, 02, 25), (2025, 05, 21))]", "# SAP Technology Updates Overview as of January 2024\n\nThis report provides an overview of key technology updates within SAP, focusing on components such as Kyma Runtime, UI Theme Designer, ABAP Environment, and Continuous Integration & Delivery. The information highlights the importance of these updates in enhancing the company's technology infrastructure and improving user experience. The report is relevant to SAP's technology operations around January 2024.\n\n## Kyma Runtime Updates\n\nThe Kyma Runtime component at SAP has undergone several updates, including the release of version 1.7.0 of the Telemetry module, version 2.1.1 of the API Gateway module, and an upcoming upgrade to Kubernetes 1.27. These updates aim to improve the component's functionality, security, and user experience. Effective management of the Kyma Runtime is essential for ensuring the smooth operation of SAP's technology infrastructure and supporting the company's strategic decision-making processes. [Data: Sources (158, 159, 3600), Date_Range ((2024, 01, 15), (2024, 01, 29))]\n\n## UI Theme Designer Enhancements\n\nThe UI Theme Designer component has been updated to version 11.11.0, providing improved theming content for Cloud Foundry and Neo environments. This update enhances the user experience and allows for better customization of the UI. The UI Theme Designer plays a crucial role in maintaining SAP's brand consistency and user-friendliness, underscoring the company's commitment to delivering high-quality products. [Data: Sources (159, 3600), Date_Range ((2024, 01, 01), (2024, 01, 29))]\n\n## ABAP Environment Improvements\n\nThe ABAP Environment component has been updated to version 2402, enabling static downscaling of SAP HANA Cloud instances. This update improves the component's functionality and allows for more efficient resource management. Effective management of the ABAP Environment is essential for ensuring the smooth operation of SAP's technology infrastructure and supporting the company's strategic decision-making processes. [Data: Sources (159, 3600), Date_Range ((2024, 01, 29), (2024, 01, 29))]\n\n## Continuous Integration & Delivery Enhancements\n\nThe Continuous Integration & Delivery component has been updated to improve connectivity with on-premises Sonar instances and enable malware scans for Cloud Foundry Environment jobs. These updates enhance the component's functionality and improve user experience. Effective management of the Continuous Integration & Delivery component is essential for ensuring the smooth operation of SAP's technology infrastructure and supporting the company's strategic decision-making processes. [Data: Sources (159, 3600), Date_Range ((2024, 01, 29), (2024, 01, 29))]", "# SAP Cloud Services Overview as of December 2024\n\nThis report provides an overview of SAP's cloud services, highlighting key components, their environments, and recent updates. The information is relevant to SAP's cloud infrastructure as of December 2024.\n\n## SAP Build Process Automation Updates\n\nSAP Build Process Automation has been updated to include a filtered actions view, allowing users to directly search for Remote Function Call actions. This feature is now available in the Cloud Foundry environment. The update also includes a new 'Browse All Actions' button, replacing the former 'Browse Library' button. For more information, see Add an Action to a Process. [Data: Sources (89), Date_Range ((2024, 12, 05), (2024, 12, 05))]\n\n## Kyma Runtime Telemetry Module Update\n\nThe Kyma Runtime telemetry module has been updated to version 1.28.0, bringing several improvements, including better filtering of Istio traces, new metric pipeline resources, and improved resource configuration of the log agent. These updates are now available in the Kyma environment. [Data: Sources (90), Date_Range ((2024, 11, 20), (2024, 12, 04))]\n\n## SAP Document AI Availability in New Regions\n\nSAP Document AI is now available in the Amazon Web Services region ap11 - Asia Pacific (Singapore) and the Microsoft Azure region ap20 - Australia (Sydney). These updates are now available in the Cloud Foundry environment. [Data: Sources (91, 92), Date_Range ((2024, 12, 04), (2024, 12, 04))]\n\n## SAP Task Center Improvements\n\nSAP Task Center has been improved with better caching for service and task provider destinations, optimizing access, database usage, and performance. Internal refactoring and optimizations related to concurrency issues have also been addressed. These updates are now available in the Cloud Foundry environment. [Data: Sources (93, 94, 95), Date_Range ((2024, 12, 04), (2024, 12, 04))]\n\n## Cloud Identity Services Updates\n\nCloud Identity Services has been updated with several new features, including the ability to assign authorization policies to users, allowing them to access only source systems, target systems, proxy systems, provisioning logs, or any combination of these. These updates are now available in the Cloud Foundry, Kyma, and Neo environments. [Data: Sources (96, 97, 98), Date_Range ((2024, 12, 03), (2024, 12, 03))]", "# SAP Cloud Foundry and SAP BTP Overview as of March 2025\n\nThis report delves into SAP Cloud Foundry and SAP BTP's key components, illustrating how these entities interact within the organizational framework to provide a robust and secure platform for SAP applications. The information is relevant to the company's operations around mid-2025.\n\n## Cloud Foundry Updates\n\nCloud Foundry has been updated from version 48.0.0 to 48.1.0, introducing several enhancements and bug fixes. This update is crucial for maintaining the stability and security of SAP applications running on Cloud Foundry. The update includes improvements to the Tomcat 10 component, SAP HANA Driver, and SLF4J component, among others. [Data: Sources (242, 243), Date_Range ((2025, 03, 06), (2025, 03, 20))]\n\n## SAP BTP Updates\n\nSAP BTP has introduced several updates, including the removal of the old trust configuration screen and the introduction of new features in the Destination service REST API. These updates are crucial for maintaining the security and stability of SAP applications running on SAP BTP. The updates include improvements to the trust and federation process, destination service, and custom domain manager, among others. [Data: Sources (588, 1187, 1188, 1189, 1190), Date_Range ((2025, 03, 06), (2025, 03, 20))]\n\n## SAP Build Apps Updates\n\nSAP Build Apps has introduced several updates, including the removal of the option to upload the iOS distribution certificate and the introduction of a new context menu. These updates are crucial for maintaining the security and stability of SAP applications running on SAP Build Apps. The updates include improvements to the governance and security process, user experience, and application development process, among others. [Data: Sources (1192, 1193, 1194, 1195, 1196), Date_Range ((2025, 03, 06), (2025, 03, 20))]", "# SAP BTP Cloud Foundry Overview as of 2023-11-02\n\nThis report delves into SAP BTP Cloud Foundry's key components, illustrating how these entities interact within the organizational framework to uphold regulatory standards and manage financial risks effectively. The information is relevant to the company's operations around mid-2023.\n\n## Cloud Foundry Updates\n\nCloud Foundry has been updated from version 32.11.0 to 32.13.0 [Data: Sources (1, 3), Date_Range ((2023, 11, 02), (2023, 11, 02))]. This update includes various bug fixes and improvements to the platform. The new version also includes support for SAPUI5 version 1.120 [Data: Source (6), Date_Range ((2023, 11, 01), (2023, 11, 02))].\n\n## SAPUI5 Distribution 1.120\n\nSAPUI5 version 1.120 has been released for UI development and can now be consumed by SAP BTP services [Data: Source (6), Date_Range ((2023, 11, 01), (2023, 11, 02))]. This new version includes various bug fixes and improvements to the platform. The SAP Build Work Zone, standard edition, plans to consume the new SAPUI5 version as of November 16, 2023 [Data: Source (3), Date_Range ((2023, 11, 01), (2023, 11, 02))].\n\n## HTTP Request Compliance\n\nTo prevent HTTP Desync Attack, we now identify and block non-compliant HTTP requests [Data: Source (7), Date_Range ((2023, 10, 30), (2023, 11, 02))]. This security measure is available in all regions in the Neo environment except US West (Chandler) (neo-us2), Europe (Rot) (neo-eu1), Europe (Frankfurt) (neo-eu2), and China (Shanghai) (neo-cn1) [Data: Source (7), Date_Range ((2023, 10, 30), (2023, 11, 02))].", "# Cloud Identity Services and Identity Provisioning Overview as of September 2024\n\nThis report delves into the key components of Cloud Identity Services and Identity Provisioning, highlighting their roles in ensuring secure and efficient identity management within the organizational framework. The information is relevant to the company's operations around September 2024.\n\n## Cloud Identity Services Operational Scope\n\nCloud Identity Services at the company plays a pivotal role in managing identities and access to cloud-based resources. Their proactive approach, highlighted from the beginning of 2024, helps safeguard the company against potential security risks and ensures continuous compliance with evolving security standards. Effective identity management not only prevents security breaches but also supports the company's strategic decision-making processes. [Data: Sources (586, 2207), Date_Range ((2024, 01, 01), (2024, 09, 25))]\n\n## Identity Provisioning and Governance\n\nThe Identity Provisioning component ensures that all identities within the company adhere to the security standards set by regulatory bodies. Their focus on transformation expressions and delta load markers, noted starting September 2024, is crucial in maintaining the company's reputation and operational security, especially in managing complex identity transformations and delta load markers. Their efforts underscore the commitment to upholding high security standards and ethical practices. [Data: Sources (2205, 2219), Date_Range ((2024, 09, 25), (2024, 09, 25))]\n\n## Interdepartmental Collaboration for Identity Management\n\nCollaboration between Cloud Identity Services and Identity Provisioning ensures that identity management strategies are secure and efficient. This synergy is vital for holistic identity management and has been instrumental in integrating identity management with security strategies at the company. Enhanced interdepartmental cooperation during this period plays a crucial role in aligning the company's strategies with security requirements. [Data: Sources (2207, 2208), Date_Range ((2024, 09, 25), (2024, 09, 25))]"], "parameters": {"model": "text-embedding-3-small"}}, "key": "embeddings_84feb7cf6698fca50c498a826b163cc71aefb9c47010e95ea530c510a1141fac_v2"}